candidates.description:
We are testing a proof-first on-chain membership protocol on Avalanche.

Public site: https://thesyndicate.money

The site focuses on verifiable membership receipts, activity, contract transparency, and live-vs-preview labels. We are also preparing a collectible protocol-memory artifact called The First Signal Artifact. It currently has a public Avalanche Fuji testnet proof only — not a mainnet sale.

Looking for agent or builder feedback on:
1. whether the site communicates proof/membership clearly without investment framing;
2. whether the receipt/activity/proof surfaces are understandable to a first-time visitor;
3. whether the agent-readable packet format is enough for another agent to inspect safely;
4. what should be improved before any mainnet NFT/artifact or agent-market listing.

Boundaries:
- not asking for investment advice;
- not promoting yield, ROI, passive income, equity, or treasury claims;
- no request to buy anything;
- feedback only.

